1
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:03,100
"Kiss or Kill"

2
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:06,000
(Episode 2)

3
00:01:13,959 --> 00:01:14,959
I'm here.

4
00:01:15,560 --> 00:01:17,000
You think you can just walk away?

5
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:31,120
I'm just here to do business.

6
00:01:33,079 --> 00:01:34,079
There's no need for this.

7
00:01:39,799 --> 00:01:40,799
You bastard.

8
00:01:41,359 --> 00:01:43,318
You dare point a knife at me?

9
00:01:43,652 --> 00:01:45,173
You have a death wish.

10
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:47,760
Enough!

11
00:01:48,439 --> 00:01:49,439
Stay out of this.

12
00:01:49,599 --> 00:01:50,878
I'm gonna kill him today.

13
00:01:50,879 --> 00:01:52,400
Nobody points a knife at me and lives.

14
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,079
Kill him!

15
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:56,560
Lead the way.

16
00:01:57,400 --> 00:01:59,400
I have plenty of ways to make him talk.

17
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:00,680
That won't be necessary.

18
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:02,719
This guy...

19
00:02:03,359 --> 00:02:04,359
I'll interrogate him.

20
00:02:04,799 --> 00:02:05,799
What do you mean?

21
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:07,400
You're too heavy-handed.

22
00:02:07,519 --> 00:02:08,639
If you ruin our lead,

23
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:10,280
it's bad for all of us.

24
00:02:10,960 --> 00:02:12,120
He's my prisoner.

25
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:13,599
He belongs to Lin.

26
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:21,840
Where's the interrogation?
I'll take him there.

27
00:02:22,719 --> 00:02:25,319
I suggest you don't cause trouble.

28
00:02:31,479 --> 00:02:32,960
Brother Scorpion, what do we do?

29
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:35,000
Didn't you hear what the kid said?

30
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:37,240
Don't cause trouble.

31
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:38,240
Yes, sir.

32
00:02:47,159 --> 00:02:48,360
He's a tough one.

33
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:54,520
One more kick and he's done for.

34
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:56,240
Come on, you interrogate him.

35
00:02:59,719 --> 00:03:00,520
Get out.

36
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:01,520
Why should I?

37
00:03:02,879 --> 00:03:04,159
You know exactly why.

38
00:03:04,439 --> 00:03:05,560
When it comes to this,

39
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:07,280
I'm better at it than you.

40
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:14,840
I'm only giving you half an hour.

41
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:24,240
Looks like

42
00:03:25,639 --> 00:03:27,680
you've had a rough trip.

43
00:03:28,039 --> 00:03:29,879
You should have expected that.

44
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:33,800
What I didn't expect is

45
00:03:34,759 --> 00:03:37,400
what exactly you're here for.

46
00:03:38,639 --> 00:03:40,199
To do business, of course.

47
00:03:42,439 --> 00:03:43,439
Is that so?

48
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:45,240
What else?

49
00:03:46,919 --> 00:03:47,919
As for you,

50
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:49,080
you look like

51
00:03:49,081 --> 00:03:50,401
a top executive of the Lin Group.

52
00:03:50,639 --> 00:03:52,000
Don't tell me you're the boss.

53
00:03:58,759 --> 00:03:59,919
I guessed right.

54
00:04:00,439 --> 00:04:01,560
Boss Lin.

55
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:05,199
Is this how you treat your guests?

56
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:08,840
You're a mercenary.

57
00:04:10,039 --> 00:04:11,599
What kind of business are you here for?

58
00:04:12,879 --> 00:04:14,120
Even mercenaries

59
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:16,000
want to score big.

60
00:04:18,920 --> 00:04:20,759
Still being a smartass.

61
00:04:21,759 --> 00:04:23,000
I control the routes.

62
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:24,480
You can test them anytime.

63
00:04:25,759 --> 00:04:26,839
Let me ask you.

64
00:04:27,639 --> 00:04:29,279
Who is your employer?

65
00:04:30,439 --> 00:04:31,439
Or rather,

66
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:35,560
who is your target?

67
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:42,720
What if my target is you?

68
00:04:44,720 --> 00:04:46,319
Then before you make a move,

69
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:51,680
I'll take your life first.

70
00:04:54,199 --> 00:04:55,199
Is that so?

71
00:04:57,720 --> 00:04:58,959
You think I won't?

72
00:04:59,959 --> 00:05:01,000
Because...

73
00:05:05,279 --> 00:05:07,560
Because three years ago,

74
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:09,480
I saved a life.

75
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:22,680
All done.

76
00:05:22,839 --> 00:05:23,919
Let's grab a drink tonight.

77
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:25,240
Keep fooling around.

78
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:26,680
The military has rules.

79
00:05:26,681 --> 00:05:27,800
I can't join you.

80
00:05:28,439 --> 00:05:29,600
That's why I say,

81
00:05:29,839 --> 00:05:31,279
freedom is the best.

82
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:38,160
Don't...

83
00:05:39,199 --> 00:05:40,240
Don't kill me!

84
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:41,560
Who are you?

85
00:05:41,839 --> 00:05:43,240
I'm a photographer.

86
00:05:43,279 --> 00:05:44,040
Someone's chasing me.

87
00:05:44,040 --> 00:05:45,040
At least six of them.

88
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:46,560
Why are they chasing you?

89
00:05:47,439 --> 00:05:48,759
They're terrorists.

90
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:50,278
I caught something on camera.

91
00:05:50,279 --> 00:05:51,279
And they spotted me.

92
00:05:51,839 --> 00:05:52,839
Get down!

93
00:06:01,720 --> 00:06:02,560
Three on the left.

94
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:03,319
Two on the right.

95
00:06:03,319 --> 00:06:04,040
More in the back.

96
00:06:04,041 --> 00:06:05,239
How many did you say were chasing you?

97
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:06,240
Six.

98
00:06:06,519 --> 00:06:07,959
But two more just showed up.

99
00:06:13,079 --> 00:06:14,360
You sure kept a good count.

100
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:20,958
I'll push the left.

101
00:06:20,959 --> 00:06:22,879
You cover me. Can you do that?

102
00:06:23,959 --> 00:06:25,639
I think so.

103
00:06:28,839 --> 00:06:29,839
Know how to use it?

104
00:06:30,639 --> 00:06:31,680
I'll try.

105
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:46,480
You've got some skills.

106
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:47,480
Right back at you.

107
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:50,199
Two at ten o'clock.

108
00:06:50,639 --> 00:06:51,879
Two at two o'clock.

109
00:06:52,519 --> 00:06:53,639
You take left, I take right.

110
00:06:59,839 --> 00:07:00,839
Not bad, huh?

111
00:07:02,160 --> 00:07:03,160
Watch out!

112
00:07:04,279 --> 00:07:05,359
I'm sorry.

113
00:07:05,360 --> 00:07:06,439
I was careless.

114
00:07:07,240 --> 00:07:08,240
Two more left.

115
00:07:08,279 --> 00:07:09,839
Behind the oil barrels at ten o'clock.

116
00:07:18,240 --> 00:07:19,240
We're clear.

117
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:29,480
No.

118
00:07:31,240 --> 00:07:33,759
The gunshots definitely
alerted more of them.

119
00:07:39,439 --> 00:07:40,559
I'm getting you out of here.

120
00:07:46,480 --> 00:07:47,480
Stay awake.

121
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:50,239
I'm awake.

122
00:07:50,240 --> 00:07:51,720
Just a little tired.

123
00:07:52,319 --> 00:07:53,519
We just met.

124
00:07:54,199 --> 00:07:55,639
At least you should let me know

125
00:07:55,920 --> 00:07:57,160
who you really are.

126
00:07:57,879 --> 00:08:01,279
A combat photographer.

127
00:08:01,959 --> 00:08:02,959
Yeah, right.

128
00:08:07,319 --> 00:08:08,319
Hold on tight.

129
00:08:57,120 --> 00:08:58,519
Who are you, really?

130
00:08:59,559 --> 00:09:00,720
I told you.

131
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:03,039
A combat photographer.

132
00:09:03,759 --> 00:09:05,320
A combat photographer

133
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:06,879
doesn't shoot that well.

134
00:09:08,279 --> 00:09:09,440
Let alone kill people.

135
00:09:13,759 --> 00:09:15,119
But that doesn't matter right now.

136
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:26,080
You need to treat that wound immediately.

137
00:09:41,919 --> 00:09:42,919
Bite down on this.

138
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:52,120
Bear with it.

139
00:09:59,639 --> 00:10:00,639
Don't move.

140
00:10:02,080 --> 00:10:03,159
The more you cooperate,

141
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:04,679
the less it'll hurt.

142
00:11:09,279 --> 00:11:10,279
Go check inside.

143
00:11:45,879 --> 00:11:46,879
I'm surprised.

144
00:11:47,320 --> 00:11:48,480
You didn't even make a sound.

145
00:11:50,159 --> 00:11:51,559
I was afraid your hands would shake

146
00:11:52,120 --> 00:11:53,320
and you'd stitch it crooked.

147
00:12:24,879 --> 00:12:26,239
Good technique.

148
00:12:26,240 --> 00:12:27,240
Lots of practice.

149
00:12:28,919 --> 00:12:30,240
You're from the military.

150
00:12:31,600 --> 00:12:32,600
Good eye.

151
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:34,360
Spending years in war zones,

152
00:12:35,039 --> 00:12:36,120
I've seen a lot.

153
00:12:36,559 --> 00:12:37,559
However,

154
00:12:37,879 --> 00:12:39,440
you're definitely different from them.

155
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:41,000
How so?

156
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:42,240
Am I more handsome?

157
00:12:42,639 --> 00:12:43,879
You're more unruly.

158
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:46,759
A mercenary who works for money

159
00:12:47,080 --> 00:12:48,080
doesn't need rules.

160
00:12:49,240 --> 00:12:50,559
Just a mercenary?

161
00:12:52,879 --> 00:12:54,080
Six years ago,

162
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:56,039
I was a proper border guard.

163
00:12:57,440 --> 00:12:58,720
Why did you quit?

164
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:03,360
During a mission once,

165
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:05,518
intel said

166
00:13:05,519 --> 00:13:07,279
it was a militant stronghold.

167
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:09,159
But I saw

168
00:13:09,879 --> 00:13:12,480
women and children in the village.

169
00:13:12,919 --> 00:13:14,200
If the airstrike hit,

170
00:13:15,399 --> 00:13:16,600
they would all die.

171
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:19,240
So you...

172
00:13:19,799 --> 00:13:21,120
You disobeyed orders.

173
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:23,000
I led my team

174
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,798
and snuck in on foot.

175
00:13:25,799 --> 00:13:26,960
We saved most of them.

176
00:13:28,519 --> 00:13:30,080
But there were still a few

177
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:31,600
who didn't make it out.

178
00:14:20,136 --> 00:14:21,603
[Discharge order]

179
00:14:33,440 --> 00:14:34,960
You saved those people,

180
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:37,039
but lost your military status.

181
00:14:37,919 --> 00:14:39,000
Do you regret it?

182
00:14:40,120 --> 00:14:41,120
No regrets.

183
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:43,200
When we were evacuating,

184
00:14:43,201 --> 00:14:44,759
a kid turned back and smiled at me.

185
00:14:45,039 --> 00:14:46,039
I knew right then

186
00:14:47,039 --> 00:14:48,039
it was worth it.

187
00:14:48,960 --> 00:14:49,879
What if that kid

188
00:14:49,880 --> 00:14:51,200
was also a militant?

189
00:14:58,120 --> 00:14:59,320
You mean

190
00:14:59,799 --> 00:15:01,879
a kid who could barely speak?

191
00:15:03,799 --> 00:15:05,000
You never know.

192
00:15:09,799 --> 00:15:11,360
What on earth have you been through

193
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:15,000
to make you think like that?

194
00:15:15,519 --> 00:15:16,799
As a combat photographer,

195
00:15:17,519 --> 00:15:18,759
I've documented a lot.

196
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:21,440
Naturally, I overthink.

197
00:15:22,879 --> 00:15:24,120
If you think so much,

198
00:15:24,600 --> 00:15:26,200
didn't you ever think I might hurt you?

199
00:15:28,399 --> 00:15:29,559
If you were going to hurt me,

200
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:31,680
you wouldn't have opened fire for me.

201
00:15:33,320 --> 00:15:35,120
Are all photographers as smart as you?

202
00:15:35,759 --> 00:15:37,000
It seems I guessed right.

203
00:15:39,120 --> 00:15:40,279
What do you think?

204
00:15:42,759 --> 00:15:43,759
I don't know.

205
00:16:27,039 --> 00:16:28,519
Ran into a little situation just now.

206
00:16:28,679 --> 00:16:30,559
Minor issue. It's handled.

207
00:16:32,879 --> 00:16:33,879
I have to go.

208
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:35,399
You still haven't told me.

209
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:37,360
What's your name?

210
00:16:40,159 --> 00:16:41,360
Just call me A-yang.

211
00:16:43,399 --> 00:16:44,840
Doesn't sound like a real name.

212
00:16:46,840 --> 00:16:48,320
Would you tell me your real name?

213
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,000
I'm...

214
00:16:53,399 --> 00:16:54,399
Nie Chuan.

215
00:17:01,240 --> 00:17:02,440
Let me have this.

216
00:17:04,240 --> 00:17:05,240
No way.

217
00:17:10,039 --> 00:17:11,720
I did save your life, after all.

218
00:17:12,079 --> 00:17:13,319
I deserve some kind of reward.

219
00:17:21,559 --> 00:17:22,839
You'll regret this.

220
00:17:50,799 --> 00:17:51,799
I told you.

221
00:17:52,319 --> 00:17:53,519
You'd regret it.

222
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:55,000
Regret what?

223
00:17:55,440 --> 00:17:57,160
Regret messing with you three years ago?

224
00:17:57,319 --> 00:17:58,519
Or regret...

225
00:17:58,960 --> 00:18:00,480
falling into your hands now?

226
00:18:05,839 --> 00:18:07,119
I really misjudged you.

227
00:18:08,359 --> 00:18:09,799
You change your tune pretty fast.

228
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:10,960
Tell me.

229
00:18:11,359 --> 00:18:12,359
How did you misjudge me?

230
00:18:13,240 --> 00:18:14,558
I was blind.

231
00:18:14,559 --> 00:18:15,680
If I had known earlier...

232
00:18:15,920 --> 00:18:17,200
that you were such a big boss...

233
00:18:17,559 --> 00:18:18,400
back then...

234
00:18:18,401 --> 00:18:19,599
I wouldn't have let you go.

235
00:18:23,240 --> 00:18:24,599
Then starting today...

236
00:18:25,200 --> 00:18:26,280
You're staying at my place.

237
00:18:27,440 --> 00:18:28,640
So you agree to hire me?

238
00:18:31,640 --> 00:18:32,759
Boss Lin.

239
00:18:36,359 --> 00:18:37,839
I don't trust your route.

240
00:18:38,240 --> 00:18:40,000
And I trust you even less.

241
00:18:41,039 --> 00:18:44,400
So it's imprisonment?

242
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:47,960
It's a deal.

243
00:18:51,240 --> 00:18:52,240
A deal?

244
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:53,680
Then what do I get out of it?

245
00:18:54,680 --> 00:18:55,920
You give me the route.

246
00:18:56,680 --> 00:18:57,960
I keep you alive.

247
00:18:58,759 --> 00:19:01,680
Sounds like I'm getting
the short end of the stick.

248
00:19:04,599 --> 00:19:05,599
You can leave.

249
00:19:07,839 --> 00:19:08,920
I'm not leaving.

250
00:19:09,319 --> 00:19:10,559
Leaving would be a bigger loss.

251
00:19:11,640 --> 00:19:13,680
Originally, it was for the money.

252
00:19:14,359 --> 00:19:15,559
But now...

253
00:19:16,440 --> 00:19:18,519
Things are getting interesting.

254
00:19:20,720 --> 00:19:22,160
Since you want to stay...

255
00:19:23,079 --> 00:19:24,079
Then...

256
00:19:24,680 --> 00:19:25,680
As you wish.

257
00:19:40,960 --> 00:19:43,359
Is this how the Lin family treats its guests?

258
00:19:43,559 --> 00:19:44,839
I did save your life, you know.

259
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:47,680
It's not bad.

260
00:19:47,839 --> 00:19:48,999
At least you get to sit on the couch.

261
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:50,000
Is this your place?

262
00:19:50,960 --> 00:19:53,879
So luxurious and comfortable.

263
00:19:53,880 --> 00:19:54,960
Look up.

264
00:19:55,839 --> 00:19:57,079
So direct?

265
00:19:57,799 --> 00:19:58,839
You talk too much.

266
00:19:59,039 --> 00:20:01,079
Guess you didn't get beaten enough.

267
00:20:25,397 --> 00:20:26,397
Easy.

268
00:20:26,766 --> 00:20:28,565
Are you disinfecting or torturing me?

269
00:20:31,965 --> 00:20:34,366
If you're afraid of pain, behave.

270
00:20:38,759 --> 00:20:40,799
You used to be so gentle.

271
00:20:43,880 --> 00:20:45,680
You didn't use to be this annoying.

272
00:21:02,039 --> 00:21:03,039
A-yang.

273
00:21:03,799 --> 00:21:05,039
Or should I say...

274
00:21:07,599 --> 00:21:08,599
Lin Yan.

275
00:21:11,160 --> 00:21:12,319
Lin Yan.

276
00:21:14,559 --> 00:21:16,079
Finally know your real name.

277
00:21:17,240 --> 00:21:19,839
I'm still Nie Chuan.

278
00:21:21,680 --> 00:21:22,960
Nie Chuan the mercenary?

279
00:21:23,279 --> 00:21:24,679
Or Nie Chuan the guide?

280
00:21:24,680 --> 00:21:25,279
Both.

281
00:21:25,440 --> 00:21:26,680
I'm very honest.

282
00:21:26,839 --> 00:21:28,240
Unlike some people.

283
00:21:29,680 --> 00:21:30,720
So hypocritical.

284
00:21:45,680 --> 00:21:47,759
Got it, Second Uncle. Understood.
